      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5a7ef34e0238de350e4dc63e|full_name}: I haven't tried in a while, but I can safely assume that serialization is still broken, and that most return objects have indexed properties, meaning anything with an object return value is still broken. (So pretty much every function) There were some function calls that when made with any value would immidiately cause the game to hang, and subsequently crash. As I only knew about any of this back before the game was obfuscated, I can't really say much on the state of the API now.\nTBH, I'm just interested someone responded to this. I may poke around again with my webpage js REPL console tool to see what I can find.",
